--- body ---

## Context

Two files independently implement the same "read a Zotero profile's
`extensions.json` and report present/absent/unreadable, tolerant of
every wrong shape" logic: `bench/sdt_sitter_install.py`'s
`read_addon_record` (hardened through three review rounds under ticket
0688/PR #373) and `bench/acceptance/adapters/beaver.py`'s
`_host_addon_record` (the identical fix hand-ported under ticket
0712/PR #383). This is now the second time the same four-defect fix
(document-shape, container-shape, element-shape guards plus
`RecursionError` on deep nesting) has had to be hand-duplicated between
these two files, with nothing tracking the divergence risk. If a third
adapter grows the same pattern, or either file's shape contract
changes, this will silently drift.

Both PRs' own review explicitly considered and deferred extraction: a
shared helper wasn't taken because `bench/sdt_sitter_install.py` is a
standalone CLI script for one specific plugin, not a shared library,
and `bench/acceptance/adapters/beaver.py` is a different plugin's
acceptance adapter -- importing one into the other creates an odd
cross-plugin coupling. Ticket 0712's Imagine-phase note observed that
`read_addon_record` is already a free function parametrized on
`profile`/`addon_id` (not bound to `self.profile`), so extraction is
mechanically easy; the objection is architectural, not technical.

## Work

- Decide the right home for a shared reader: a new neutral module
  (e.g. `bench/host_addon_record.py`) that both `bench/sdt_sitter_install.py`
  and `bench/acceptance/adapters/beaver.py` import, parametrized on
  `profile: Path` and `addon_id: str`.
- Port both files' call sites to the shared function; delete the
  duplicated logic from each.
- Merge both files' test suites for this function's shape-guard
  behavior (`tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`'s three shape tests and
  `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_beaver.py`'s section-11 tests) into
  one shared test module, or keep both but assert they exercise the
  same shared function.
- Confirm no caller relies on a behavioral difference between the two
  current implementations before merging them (a quick diff of the two
  functions' bodies as of this ticket's filing should be identical
  modulo the `self`/parameter binding).

## Acceptance

- [x] One function implements the shape-guarded `extensions.json`
      reader; both `bench/sdt_sitter_install.py` and
      `bench/acceptance/adapters/beaver.py` call it —
      `host_addon_record(profile, addon_id)` in `bench/host_addon_record.py`,
      imported at `bench/sdt_sitter_install.py:45` and
      `bench/acceptance/adapters/beaver.py:164`; both former bodies are now
      one-line delegations (`sdt_sitter_install.py:67`, `beaver.py:947`).
- [x] No behavior regression: all existing tests for both call sites
      still pass (or their shared replacement covers the same cases) —
      `tests/test_host_addon_record.py` carries the merged shape-guard suite
      against the shared function, plus two delegation arms
      (`:268`, `:284`) that monkeypatch a spy into each module and assert the
      call site actually reaches it; `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_beaver.py`
      keeps its section-11 tests through `_host_addon_record`.
- [x] `make check` green.

## Scope

Low priority, low severity -- pure duplication-reduction, not a bug.
Cheap to defer further; file exists so the divergence stops being
silent.

